{"package":"ConvertUnixTimestamp","version":"0.1.1","assessment":"complete","packageSha256":"7caecb3d1928c26cd7c26de9dbc026cea1b04c1a3a2a588ba9259132619c99dc","scannedAt":"2026-10-24T09:14:56.317Z","scannerVersion":"0.1.0","rulesetVersion":"0.3.0","tools":{"powerShell":"7.6.8","psscriptAnalyzer":"1.25.0","psscriptAnalyzerExpected":"1.25.0","clamav":null},"packageUrl":"https://www.powershellgallery.com/packages/ConvertUnixTimestamp/0.1.1","metadata":{"title":"ConvertUnixTimestamp","description":"Apteco PS Modules - PowerShell unix timestamp conversion\r\n\r\nConverts a [DateTime] into a numeric unix timestamp as [UInt64] and vice versa.\r\n\r\nTo get a unix timestamp from a [DateTime]::Now or (Get-Date) just do it like in these examples\r\n\r\nGet-Unixtime\r\nGet-Unixtime -InMilliseconds\r\nGet-Unixtime -InMilliseconds -Timestamp ( Get-Date ).AddDays(-2)\r\n\r\nTo convert a timestamp back, just do it like here\r\n\r\nConvertFrom-UnixTime -Unixtime 1591775090\r\nConvertFrom-UnixTime -Unixtime 1591775090 -ConvertToLocalTimezone\r\nConvertFrom-UnixTime -Unixtime 1591775146091 -InMilliseconds\r\n( ConvertFrom-UnixTime -Unixtime $lastSession.timestamp ).ToString(\"yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mm:ssK\")\r","authors":"florian.von.bracht@apteco.de","owners":"apteco_fvb","projectUrl":"https://github.com/Apteco/AptecoPSModules/tree/main/ConvertUnixTimestamp","publishedAt":"2025-10-01T13:35:17.35","updatedAt":"2026-10-22T19:40:01.42","tags":["powershell","PSEdition_Desktop","PSEdition_Core","Windows","Linux","Apteco","PSModule","PSFunction_Get-Unixtime","PSCommand_Get-Unixtime","PSFunction_ConvertFrom-Unixtime","PSCommand_ConvertFrom-Unixtime","PSIncludes_Function"]},"dependencies":[],"fileInventory":[{"path":"_rels/.rels","size":514,"crc32":"6cc274c6","extension":"rels"},{"path":"ConvertUnixTimestamp.nuspec","size":1848,"crc32":"e91e65da","extension":"nuspec"},{"path":"Public/Get-Unixtime.ps1","size":1607,"crc32":"94002ac2","extension":"ps1"},{"path":"ConvertUnixTimestamp.psm1","size":1606,"